{"type":"message","id":"a315f219","parentId":"190f86e4","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:46:19.281Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The web search failed due to missing API key. Let me proceed based on my knowledge. I'll choose whisper.cpp or a Node.js binding. Since the requirement is for fast (<2s) and offline, whisper.cpp is excellent but requires compilation. However, for a Node.js skill, I can use @ffmpeg-installer/ffmpeg and a lightweight binding like openai-whisper or faster-whisper. Actually, whisper.cpp can be called via child_process as a command-line tool, but that might be heavy.\n\nA better approach might be to use a Node.js binding like:\n- whisper.cpp with Node bindings (e.g., whisper-node)\n- A faster alternative like Vosk (offline, fast, supports multiple languages) - but it's not Whisper\n- Or use @ffmpeg-installer/ffmpeg for conversion and a lightweight model\n\nGiven the constraints (fast, <2s for short voice notes), I'll go with whisper.cpp because it's highly optimized and fast for short audio, especially if using the tiny or tiny.en models. But we need to consider that the user wants a Node.js skill. whisper.cpp can be compiled and then called via Node's child_process or there's a whisper.cpp Node binding.\n\nActually, I should check if there are any existing skills in the workspace to understand the skill structure.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_924bf643f70b4f2baffbdcdd","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\workspace-coder2\\TOOLS.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":12760,"output":642,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13402,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771422373064}}
{"type":"message","id":"d8606172","parentId":"a315f219","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:46:19.296Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_924bf643f70b4f2baffbdcdd","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# TOOLS.md - Local Notes\n\nSkills define _how_ tools work. This file is for _your_ specifics — the stuff that's unique to your setup.\n\n## What Goes Here\n\nThings like:\n\n- Camera names and locations\n- SSH hosts and aliases\n- Preferred voices for TTS\n- Speaker/room names\n- Device nicknames\n- Anything environment-specific\n\n## Examples\n\n```markdown\n### Cameras\n\n- living-room → Main area, 180° wide angle\n- front-door → Entrance, motion-triggered\n\n### SSH\n\n- home-server → 192.168.1.100, user: admin\n\n### TTS\n\n- Preferred voice: \"Nova\" (warm, slightly British)\n- Default speaker: Kitchen HomePod\n```\n\n## Why Separate?\n\nSkills are shared. Your setup is yours. Keeping them apart means you can update skills without losing your notes, and share skills without leaking your infrastructure.\n\n---\n\nAdd whatever helps you do your job. This is your cheat sheet.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1771422379295}}
