{"type":"message","id":"fa125f26","parentId":"7aa9801d","timestamp":"2026-02-18T13:47:27.096Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! The directory was created and the manifest file was written. Now I need to create transcribe.js. Let me design it carefully:\n\n- It should use @xenova/transformers to run Whisper.\n- It should accept audio file path (OGG/Opus from WhatsApp) and optionally language.\n- It should convert the audio to WAV (16kHz, mono) using ffmpeg, as required by the model.\n- It should load the Whisper model (I'll use 'tiny' for speed; ~2s on CPU for short clips). It could also support 'base', 'small' etc via a param but not required.\n- It should return the transcribed text as JSON to stdout.\n\nThe @xenova/transformers library supports Whisper directly with the pipeline method. It expects audio as a Tensor or a file path? Actually, the pipeline can take a file path or a URL. It handles audio loading internally using the browser's or Node's audio decoding? In Node, it uses `node-wave` to read WAV files. But it might not support OGG/Opus directly. So we need to convert to a WAV file first.\n\nThus steps:\n1. Use ffmpeg to convert input audio file to 16kHz mono WAV (PCM s16le). This can be done via fluent-ffmpeg.\n2. Use the transformers pipeline for automatic-speech-recognition with a Whisper model.\n3. Run the transcription and output result.\n\nAlso, handle errors and log.\n\nThe script should be executable: `node transcribe.js --audioFile <path> [--language <code>]`.\n\nIt will output JSON: `{ \"text\": \"transcribed text\" }`.\n\nNow, I'll write transcribe.js.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create the main transcribe.js implementation:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_45ed9d4df6f544ae9b68a3bc","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env node\n\n/**\n * Transcribe Skill for OpenClaw\n * Converts audio (e.g., WhatsApp voice messages) to text using Whisper.\n * Works offline and aims for <2s transcription for short notes.\n *\n * Usage: node transcribe.js --audioFile <path> [--language <code>]\n * Example: node transcribe.js --audioFile \"voice.ogg\" --language en\n *\n * Outputs JSON to stdout: { \"text\": \"transcribed text\" }\n */\n\nconst fs = require('fs');\nconst path = require('path');\nconst { pipeline } = require('@xenova/transformers');\nconst ffmpeg = require('fluent-ffmpeg');\nconst ffmpegPath = require('@ffmpeg-installer/ffmpeg').path;\n\n// Set ffmpeg path\nffmpeg.setFfmpegPath(ffmpegPath);\n\n// Configuration - can be overridden via environment variable\nconst MODEL = process.env.WHISPER_MODEL || 'openai/whisper-tiny'; // Use tiny for fastest speed (~2s)\nconst DEVICE = process.env.WHISPER_DEVICE || 'cpu'; // 'cpu' or 'cuda' (if GPU available)\nconst TASK = 'automatic-speech-recognition';\n\n// Cache the pipeline to avoid reloading model on every call\nlet transcribePipeline = null;\n\n/**\n * Initialize the transcription pipeline\n */\nasync function getPipeline() {\n  if (transcribePipeline) return transcribePipeline;\n\n  console.error(`[Transcribe] Loading Whisper model: ${MODEL} on ${DEVICE}...`);\n  transcribePipeline = await pipeline(TASK, MODEL, {\n    device: DEVICE,\n    quantized: true, // Use quantized model for smaller size and faster inference\n  });\n  console.error('[Transcribe] Model loaded.');\n  return transcribePipeline;\n}\n\n/**\n * Convert audio file to WAV format (16kHz, mono, PCM) required by Whisper\n * Returns path to the temporary WAV file\n */\nfunction convertToWav(inputPath, outputPath) {\n  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {\n    ffmpeg(inputPath)\n      .toFormat('wav')\n      .audioFrequency(16000)\n      .audioChannels(1)\n      .audioCodec('pcm_s16le')\n      .on('end', () => {\n        resolve(outputPath);\n      })\n      .on('error', (err) => {\n        fs.unlink(outputPath, () => {}); // Cleanup\n        reject(err);\n      })\n      .save(outputPath);\n  });\n}\n\n/**\n * Transcribe audio file to text\n *\n * @param {string} audioFile - Path to the input audio (OGG, Opus, MP3, WAV, etc.)\n * @param {string} [language] - Optional language code (e.g., 'en', 'hi'). If not provided, auto-detection is used.\n * @returns {Promise<string>} Transcribed text\n */\nasync function transcribeAudio(audioFile, language) {\n  if (!fs.existsSync(audioFile)) {\n    throw new Error(`Audio file not found: ${audioFile}`);\n  }\n\n  // Get absolute paths\n  const absAudioPath = path.resolve(audioFile);\n  const tempWavPath = path.join(\n    path.dirname(absAudioPath),\n    `transcribe_temp_${Date.now()}.wav`\n  );\n\n  try {\n    // Step 1: Convert to WAV if needed\n    console.error(`[Transcribe] Converting audio to WAV...`);\n    await convertToWav(absAudioPath, tempWavPath);\n\n    // Step 2: Load pipeline (and cache)\n    const pipe = await getPipeline();\n\n    // Step 3: Run transcription\n    console.error(`[Transcribe] Transcribing...`);\n    const startTime = Date.now();\n\n    const params = {\n      audio: tempWavPath,\n    };\n    if (language) {\n      params.parameters = {\n        language: language,\n        task: 'transcribe',\n      };\n    }\n\n    const output = await pipe(params);\n    const text = typeof output === 'string' ? output : (output.text || output[0]?.text || '');\n\n    const duration = ((Date.now() - startTime) / 1000).toFixed(2);\n    console.error(`[Transcribe] Completed in ${duration}s`);\n\n    return text.trim();\n  } finally {\n    // Cleanup temp WAV file\n    if (fs.existsSync(tempWavPath)) {\n      fs.unlink(tempWavPath, (err) => {\n        if (err) console.error('[Transcribe] Failed to delete temp file:', err);\n      });\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n/**\n * Parse command line arguments\n */\nfunction parseArgs() {\n  const args = process.argv.slice(2);\n  const options = { audioFile: null, language: null };\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < args.length; i++) {\n    if (args[i] === '--audioFile' && i + 1 < args.length) {\n      options.audioFile = args[++i];\n    } else if (args[i] === '--language' && i + 1 < args.length) {\n      options.language = args[++i];\n    }\n  }\n\n  return options;\n}\n\n// If run directly from command line\nif (require.main === module) {\n  const { audioFile, language } = parseArgs();\n\n  if (!audioFile) {\n    console.error('Error: --audioFile is required');\n    process.exit(1);\n  }\n\n  transcribeAudio(audioFile, language)\n    .then(text => {\n      // Output result as JSON to stdout\n      console.log(JSON.stringify({ text }));\n    })\n    .catch(err => {\n      console.error('Error:', err.message);\n      process.exit(1);\n    });\n}\n\n// Export for programmatic use\nmodule.exports = { transcribeAudio, getPipeline };","file_path":"D:\\workspace\\appDev\\openclaw\\.openclaw-state\\workspace\\skills\\transcribe\\transcribe.js"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"stepfun/step-3.5-flash:free","usage":{"input":16927,"output":2094,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19021,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1771422434342}}
